  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oil in a large Dutch oven over medium-high heat. Pat the lamb dry and season it with the salt and pepper.",
    "Brown the lamb in the pot in two batches, about 5 minutes per batch. Move the browned lamb to a plate.",
    "Lower the heat to medium. Add the onion and cook for 5 minutes, until soft.",
    "Stir in the garlic, cumin, ginger, cinnamon, and paprika. Cook for 30 seconds until fragrant.",
    "Add the tomatoes, water, and the lamb with any juices. Scrape up the browned bits from the bottom of the pot.",
    "Bring to a boil, then cover and reduce to low. Simmer for 35 minutes.",
    "Stir in the carrots and chickpeas. Cover and simmer for 20 to 25 minutes, until the carrots are tender and the lamb is easily pierced with a fork.",
    "Stir in the cilantro. Taste and add more salt if needed. Cool leftovers fully before storing in the fridge for 4 days or the freezer for 3 months."
